Workspace sprawl is usually governance debt in disguise.

A useful Microsoft 365 lifecycle review should record:
- the workspace's current business purpose;
- at least one accountable owner;
- members, guests, and permission structure;
- sharing and retention settings;
- the last meaningful activity;
- a decision to retain, revise, or archive.

Cloud2e's Cloud Adoption and Microsoft 365 service includes tenant governance, SharePoint and Teams architecture, sharing policies, guest-access discipline, and ongoing stewardship. Bringing those elements into one operating rhythm helps teams keep collaboration spaces aligned with current work instead of letting old sites and channels become permanent exceptions.

The goal is not to delete everything old. It is to make ownership and lifecycle decisions visible, repeatable, and reviewable.

